{#- How a bundle is handed to the workshop: which files go in, and in what
   form. Included mid-sentence by every skill that submits a local bundle, so it
   strips its own trailing newline (the closing comment below).

   The first sentence is the shared submission convention's file set: every
   `.mthds` file beneath the bundle directory except `runs/`, where
   `/pipelex-run` saves a completed run's artifacts, and every template file a
   `PipeDocGen` step names in its `template_file`, which the runner needs to load
   a bundle sent as content (`pipelex-mcp`, SPEC.md, "Template files"). The
   workshop keys each template by the step naming it and refuses one no step
   names, which is why the set is the named files and not a glob of template
   suffixes: a glob would sweep in the `method-graph.html` page `mthds_validate`
   writes beside the bundle. `pipelex-integrate` sets
   `validate_call_file_set = false` and states its own set, because the set it
   submits is the set its generated call site loads at runtime, and that is
   the call site's to define. Why `runs/` is excluded — a method that emits or
   echoes a `.mthds` file would otherwise submit its own output as source — is
   rationale, and lives in `docs/decisions.md` beside the artifact `dir`.

   `validate_call_templates` is false in `pipelex-catalog` alone: the catalog
   stores `.mthds` and `.py` files only, so `mthds_save_method` takes no template
   file, and the catalog says so at its save step. Everywhere else a template file
   goes as a path, since it has no inline form: the workshop refuses one inline,
   and one beside a bundle given inline, which is also why the inline fallback
   is a fallback only for a bundle whose steps name no template file.

   The local workshop resolves a `{ path }` item against its own working
   directory and refuses one that resolves outside it (`pipelex-mcp`,
   `src/files.ts`), an absolute path included, so the sentence names the
   refusal and its cure rather than promising that any absolute path works. It
   also reads every `{ path }` item from at or under the directory of the first
   one (SPEC.md, "Path trust boundary"), so the root `.mthds` file goes first,
   before any file or template in a subdirectory. `validate_call_root_first` is
   false in `pipelex-catalog` alone, whose save step states the same order with
   its own reason, the listed description the platform takes from the first
   file. And since a template file has no inline form, a templated bundle the
   workshop cannot read by path is a stop and the relaunch, never the inline
   fallback, which would answer that the template was not supplied.

   `validate_call_inline` is what the last sentence says of the inline form,
   after the form itself. Every skill but `pipelex-catalog` leaves it to its
   default, which calls it the fallback. The catalog sets it, because
   `mthds_save_method` is the workshop's alone and writes `pipelex-method.json`
   only beside a `{ path }` root file: for a save, the inline form is the one
   that leaves a new method unlinked, or an updated one's link behind the
   catalog. -#}
{% set validate_call_with_templates = validate_call_templates | default(true) %}
{%- if validate_call_file_set | default(true) %}Submit every `.mthds` file beneath the bundle directory **except anything under a `runs/` directory**{% if validate_call_with_templates %}, and every template file a `PipeDocGen` step names{% endif %}. {% endif %}Prefer the path form `{path: <absolute path>}`{% if validate_call_root_first | default(true) %}, **the root `.mthds` file first**, as nothing above its directory is read{% endif %}. The workshop refuses a path outside **its own** working directory, where the harness launched it; relaunching the harness from a directory holding the bundle cures that. Inline `{content, uri: <path relative to the bundle dir>}` {{ validate_call_inline | default("is the fallback for a bundle with no template file; **for a templated one, stop and ask for that relaunch**.") }}
{#- -#}
